{"id":"ALG-E02","workedExamples":[{"id":"ALG-E02-we-01","title":"Undo addition before division","steps":[{"prompt":"Solve 3x + 4 = 19. Which operation do we undo first?","reveal":"Undo the part farthest from x first. The +4 is added last, so subtract 4 from BOTH sides before touching the ×3."},{"prompt":"Subtract 4 from both sides.","reveal":"3x + 4 − 4 = 19 − 4 simplifies to 3x = 15. The balance stays level because we removed 4 from each side."},{"prompt":"Now undo the ×3. What reverses multiplication?","reveal":"Division. Divide both sides by 3: 3x ÷ 3 = 15 ÷ 3."},{"prompt":"State the solution and check it.","reveal":"x = 5. Check: 3(5) + 4 = 15 + 4 = 19. True, so x = 5."}]},{"id":"ALG-E02-we-02","title":"A negative coefficient","steps":[{"prompt":"Solve −2x + 9 = 1. What do we clear first?","reveal":"Subtract 9 from both sides first, since +9 is added last: −2x + 9 − 9 = 1 − 9 gives −2x = −8."},{"prompt":"Undo the ×(−2). Divide both sides by −2.","reveal":"−2x ÷ (−2) = −8 ÷ (−2). A negative divided by a negative is positive."},{"prompt":"Simplify and check.","reveal":"x = 4. Check: −2(4) + 9 = −8 + 9 = 1. True, so x = 4."}]}],"problems":{"p1":[{"id":"ALG-E02-p1-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-E02","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A hitter already has 7 hits and adds 2 hits each game. After g more games he has 19 hits: 2g + 7 = 19. Solve for g.","visual":"balance","answer":{"kind":"numeric","value":"6"},"misconceptionMap":{"12":"subtracted-not-divided","9.5":"divided-first","13":"sign-error-isolating"},"hints":["Clear the starting 7 hits before you divide by the per-game 2.","Subtract 7 from both sides, then divide both sides by 2."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-E02-p1-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-E02","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A player has 12 RBIs and drives in 5 more per series. After g series his total is 47 RBIs: 5g + 12 = 47. Solve for g.","visual":"balance","answer":{"kind":"numeric","value":"7"},"misconceptionMap":{"35":"